---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Category Checker" description="What Category Checker is, who it's for, and how the provider architecture works.">
  <section class="wrap flex max-w-[720px] flex-col gap-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-[36px] font-medium leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.5px] text-heading">About Category Checker</h1>

    <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Category Checker is a free MSNugget tool that checks how a website or URL is categorized across security and web
      filtering platforms. It's built for Microsoft Global Secure Access administrators, security administrators, network
      administrators, cloud architects, and IT professionals who need to validate category-based access decisions quickly.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 text-[20px] font-medium text-heading">Why it exists</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Category-based access policies (in Global Secure Access, a secure web gateway, or a firewall) only work correctly if
      every enforcement point agrees on how a domain is categorized. In practice, vendors disagree — a domain can be
      "Business" in one console and "Uncategorized" in another. Category Checker surfaces that disagreement in one place
      instead of five browser tabs.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 text-[20px] font-medium text-heading">How it works</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Every provider implements the same <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-accent">CategoryProvider</code> interface.
      Today, all five providers return mock, deterministic sample data so the interface and architecture can be built and
      validated before wiring in real vendor APIs. See
      <a href="https://msnugget.com/" class="underline hover:text-heading">msnugget.com</a> for the rest of the MSNugget
      tool family, and this project's <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-accent">ARCHITECTURE.md</code> for the technical
      design.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 text-[20px] font-medium text-heading">Independence</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Category Checker is an independent, community-built tool. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
      Microsoft, Fortinet, Cisco, Zscaler, or Netskope.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
